        ":question/id": "65c77d8f-4e68-5667-bebf-382cd66bf3e2",
        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-320965",
        ":question/problem": "![](images/45/453e8fc1c4d8a5262fd0a8aa7341dd71b909a4a72cec94cd2698f800f7dc06c9.png)\n\nLet $A(0,3)$ and $B(4,-1).$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{AB}|.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$|\\overset{\\to }{AB}|=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=0i+3j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=4i-j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{OB}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\  & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i-j)-(0i+3j) \\\\  & =4i-4j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+16} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
      },
