        ":question/problem": "![](images/b9/b911126b4468e016afbab7faaf20223d0811827bb7f57cdefc2f1923cb7faf1b.png)\n\nPoints $A$ and $C$ are shown in the picture above. Find $|\\overset{\\to }{AC}|.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "From the picture, we obtain $A(0,3)$ and $C(4,0).$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=0i+3j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OC}=c=4i+0j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AC} & =\\overset{\\to }{OC}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\  & =c-a \\\\  & =(4i)-(3j) \\\\  & =4i-3j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AC}| & =\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
